# Workflow

Code patterns live in `.cursor/rules/` and in the nearest existing feature. The user owns those patterns. Copy an existing pattern when it fits. If the change needs a new pattern, stop and ask before spreading it.

## Plan

Use Cursor Plan. The user reviews and adjusts the plan before implementation. The plan names the files to touch, the pattern to copy, and the checks to run. Do not write a parallel spec.

## Implement

One pass implements the approved plan, including tests and Storybook when that UI surface already has them. Read the plan, the matching rule, and the nearest feature. Leave product overview and auth docs unread on a local UI change.

## Validate

A later pass reads the diff against the approved plan and the relevant rules. It reports concrete gaps. It does not replan or introduce patterns. The user approves.

## Context

Read only files the plan names. Expand only when implementation cannot proceed. Do not scan the repository for general context.
